# Markdown recall, hand-labelled (#2).
#
# The precision samples are drawn from the documents edges the layer
# made; this one is drawn from what the docs say. Its population is every
# distinct inline code span of a section, outside fenced blocks, in the
# Markdown files the layer reads: 7,200 in the nine public repositories
# of markdown-sample.pxf on 2026-10-14. 120 were drawn by TestDrawSamples,
# allotted in proportion to each repository's count and taken in order of
# the SHA-256 of "repo|section|span". Each was labelled by reading its
# sentence and searching the repository:
#
#   declaration  names the declaration in "to", a node of the graph;
#   nonode       names a declaration of the repository the graph has no
#                node for;
#   test         names a test function, absent from the default graph;
#   external     names a declaration outside the repository;
#   gone         names a declaration the code does not have: removed, or
#                only proposed;
#   unclear      a reader cannot tell which declaration, if any;
#   not          names no declaration: a command, flag, value, path,
#                route, keyword, tool name, or a file name used as a
#                concept.
#
# 24 are declarations, 22 external, 3 gone, 1 unclear and 70 not. Recall
# is the share of declaration spans whose section has a documents edge to
# "to", whatever span the edge records: the linker keeps one edge per
# section and target.
#
# TestOracleGoCalls (scripts/oracle.sh) re-reads the sample for every
# repository checked out at its commit. This sample replaces one of the
# same size drawn on 2026-10-08 from 16 repositories, most of them
# private.

